## Pattern 2, share 07: yes posts

### The parent runs out of ideas for filling an ordinary day with a baby or toddler.

21 of 226 posts.

These posts ask what to do after the usual toys, books, walks and care tasks have been used up, especially as wake windows lengthen or one adult takes over the day alone. The children range from about 13 weeks to toddlers, sometimes with an older sibling; one question comes from a relative who knows feeding and changing but not how to play.

- "I’m a full-time dad now and it's the *filling the day* part that gets me. I wake up thinking I've  got a plan and then somehow it’s 10:30 and I'm out of ideas" [sr020-0071]
- "I love being with him, it just feels a tad overwhelming knowing that I have to fill every day with him mostly on my own, especially at this phase when he isn’t mobile or able to play independently at all really." [sr030-0003]
- "Unsure what flair to put this under but what are we doing with our 4 month olds as in activities or anything of that sort? I’ve been racking my brain on things to do with him because he’s at the age where he’s too young to move anywhere and doesn’t want to play with toys, but he’s old enough that he’s getting super bored and wants more fulfillment in the day." [sr049-0128]
- "Parents: I will be spending a few weeks this summer caring for our grand son, 20-21 months during that time. No screen time. Beyond the playground, duplos, puzzles, books, train set...I kind of get in a rut and run out of ideas." [sr070-0121]
- "We do get out for a walk everyday, but aside from that hour I have no clue what to do with him!!" [sr108-0023]
- "I'm a 20 year old helping my 24 year old cousin with her baby boy. The mom is out with my mom. I know how to feed him and change is diaper but like after those stuff, what should I do with him? Is it possible to play with him yet or is he too young? Help lol" [sr016-0043]

**But:** The difficulty filling time does not always mean a difficult or unhappy baby. "My son is 13 weeks old—very happy and healthy guy. His sleep is a mess right now but otherwise no complaints. He’s definitely an “easy” baby during the day." [sr030-0001]

