- "How do/did you all wear out your 18 month old?" [sr023-0073]
- "I allow him plenty of independent play throughout the day and his dad helps to get his energy out when he’s home from work. Right now he has great-grandma to interact with at home, daily bath time, a regular rotation of toys, weekly play dates, a kiddie pool… and I feel like I am still struggling to meet him where he wants to be." [sr033-0082]
- "How can I ensure I’m continuing to nurture my baby boy’s personality, energy levels, and independence? Would he benefit from structured sports and play times with other kids from the age of 2? Do any of you have a baby like this? How did you handle it?" [sr033-0085]
- "While my children do get enough time outside, I would like for my family as a whole to have a generally active lifestyle that goes beyond playing in the park.  I feel like our weekends primarily go in eating out, then chilling at home. I want my children to have an active, thriving lifestyle." [sr090-0078]
- "Hi all! As we approach Winter months - I’m looking for your favorite ways to keep your toddler stimulated. Our kiddo goes to daycare so we are looking for ways to do this on weekends and days off! What have you done that knocks them out cold for naps and sleep? Thanks, all! 😊 Kiddo is 14 months." [sr127-0137]

**But:** The family asking for a more active lifestyle already reports one to two hours of outdoor play daily. "I have 2 children - a young child and an infant . My children go to play for 1-2 hours everyday. Obviously my infant isn’t walking yet, but there’s lots to be enjoyed outdoors and he loves it." [sr090-0077]

