- "It is getting harder and harder for me because it just feels like there’s no time to breathe and take a good break till bed time..on top of this she is very very active toddler, needs constant stimulation and has to get out twice a day every day..whenever we stay in because of weather etc she goes nuts!  I guiltily dread the next day these days. I enrolled her for nursery but she doesn’t start till September. […]" [sr026-0107]
- "Before anyone asks, yes she's very active and we get out of the house everyday (mostly because I hate being at home). She has so many activities, swimming, playgroup, gymnastics. She used to nap on the way home from these but has stopped doing that since this weird phase started. I even take her to the park after these activities to try to wear her out more but no luck. She eats lunch before her nap/quiet time so her belly is always full but it doesn't seem to help." [sr084-0009]
- "I loveee the contact naps and will have as many as I can with him but I am DESPERATE to have some time during the day so I can get things done. My partner is away next week and even when he's home I only get about 5 minutes a day (not even that), I feel like it's gonna break me if I can't get him down for at least 1 nap a day!!" [sr115-0004]
- "Where do I even start? Do I gradually teach her to settle while I stay in the room and slowly work toward leaving? How do you teach a very high energy toddler to actually slow down and rest when they’ve never had to do it independently? Help please!!!!" [sr121-0063]
- "TLDR: I need advice for how to manage the long days of our LO refusing naps" [sr133-0057]

**But:** One 15-month-old reportedly sleeps through the night on days without a nap, despite the parent’s uncertainty about dropping it. "On the days she's had no nap, she's been going to bed at 7:30am and sleeping through the night. She sometimes wakes around 5am wanting cuddles because it's been cold here. One of us will climb into bed with her and she'll go straight back to sleep and doesn't wake until 8-9am." [sr084-0010]

