- "I was talking with a girlfriend over the weekend and she said that she absolutely hates the park and never goes so that’s what prompted me to ask this." [sr133-0037]
- "Everyone asks if I'm teaching my daughter to read. She's 19 months. She can't count past however many fingers she feels like holding up. However, I read the story from the books and show her pictures from Readers Digest: Family guide to nature, but still for reading there is time." [sr038-0124]
- "I have a 6 month old. I have been BEYOND blessed to have my MIL living with us for the past two months helping me take care of baby, but she’s leaving next week and I’m **scared**." [sr087-0041]
- "All of my friends/neighbors look at me in disbelief when I ask what they did to make it work; their babies loved the stroller and slept for hours in it. I see bassinet after bassinet strolling around my neighborhood. What am I missing?" [sr114-0081]
- "This is for the parents with a toddler that never stops moving, is climbing on things, is a runner and absolute ball of energy and a walking safety-hazard. If your child will sit in your lap or on a chair or the floor for more than 2 minutes without getting up to run, this post isn't for you. I have friends with toddlers that will sit quietly and colour or hang out in their lap for 30 minutes, it just isn't my child's temperament and their advice doesn't apply!" [sr086-0125]
- "Like today for example, she would not play independently at all and either wanted me holding her or playing with her. Every time my husband tried to take her from me to give me a break, she’d have a meltdown. Yet when I’m working, I can see on our cameras she plays independently when my nanny or husband watch her" [sr119-0084]

