### How they say they feel

- "I hate it. I’m looking forward to the mental overload and demand of our third newborn phase in a handful of months because this is excruciating. And the worst part is, I can’t even THINK or LEARN something new because, as is with any physical task, it’s going to get interrupted." [sr004-0153]
- "Thing is…I don’t trust anyone to do my job as mom as well as me. I can’t let it go. I can’t send them to daycare, no one will love them or know them or treat them PRECISELY as they should be treated and I feel stuck. No, trapped. I hate it." [sr004-0155]
- "I feel like I'm not stimulating his mind enough and that it could be bad for his development. I feel so guilty I haven't found something that would make him feel thrilled for a decent amount of time. Is boredom bad for babies? Any ideas? Is this a phase? Do they learn to entertain themselves eventually?" [sr019-0049]
- "I have a beautiful amazing sweet girl who is so smart and fun, but I am feeling so bored and burnt out. […] I've always been introverted and making Mom friends feels exhausting because it's just a lot for me to socialize and I don't really want to just talk about my baby all the time. […]" [sr073-0127]
- "I just feel so hopeless. When he was a newborn, every shitty phase was just a phase. Maybe a month of whatever the fuck was making both us and the little dude miserable, until the next phase. But at least we were told that the newborn stage and all it’s phases go by quickly, and it will get easier. But since he is nearly a 1 year old now, this is just how it will be for a long time now I assume. […]" [sr045-0134]
- "[…] Honestly thinking about going back to work earlier if this careies on past 6 months and I feel awful about that, but it's so hard." [sr130-0060]
- "I made the mistake of never reattempting to get my license, not realising I won’t always live in a commutable city. My anxiety and driving skills have always been terrible so it didn’t seem worth it but now I really regret it. My boy is 1.5 years old, I live in a village in a foreign country and the closest library is 10 minutes by car but buses only go every 1-2 hours and honestly I’m scared to take one. […]" [sr092-0021]
- "This is my alternative account, which is why I do not have many posts. I would post this on my main account, but I feel ashamed in a sense." [sr096-0076]
- "My son is now 14 months and life lately has been… too easy. I love my time with him so very much and I’m lucky my husband is amazingly supportive of my last minute decision to be a SAHM. I wanted to ask what anyone has done to really maximize their time with their little ones or while they sleep and to make their partner’s lives a little more stress free too? I’m a big reader and very open to any new books or theories/ideas. […]" [sr038-0007]
- "I'm quite happy that my 17 months old can develop his independent play ability, long-time focus capacity, and don't often feel boring even we don't go out everyday. We are full-time working parents and maintain screen-free environment at home. I hope it can help if someday you don't know what to do to keep them busy." [sr008-0166]
- "But I’ve found that being in constant “attentiveness & engaging” mode is exhausting. I mean this is the mode of being an in-person Miss Rachel essentially." [sr106-0061]
- "I want to “enjoy motherhood” but I feel like I don’t know how. Sure, I can turn on the TV and watch a movie with her but I know that isn’t good for her.  Other than that, I don’t know what we can both do so we are both enjoying what we are doing" [sr100-0004]

